From: Salvo Giangreco <giangrecosalvo9@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Dec 2025 15:39:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION + FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL (merged, conflict-free)

This replaces the two separate patches:
  - 0001-Enable-FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION.patch
  - 0001-Enable-FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL.patch

Both patches were generated independently against the SAME pristine
CoreRune.smali (index 3619eba0) and their hunks overlap:

  - FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION's hunk (@@ -2835,9 +2835,9 @@) rewrites
    the FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY line (v5 -> v4).
  - FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL's hunk (@@ -2839,7 +2839,7 @@) uses
    that SAME FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY line as unchanged CONTEXT,
    still expecting it to read v5.

Applied back-to-back, whichever of the two patches lands second no
longer finds the context it expects (v4 where it wants v5, or vice
versa for FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL depending on order), so the
second patch either fails outright or is applied with fuzz against
the wrong assumption. On devices that fall into the
"SOURCE_HAS_QHD_DISPLAY=false / TARGET_HAS_QHD_DISPLAY=true" branch
(native-QHD "Plus" panels), FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL is the flag
that actually lets WindowManager honor a runtime resolution change;
FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION only controls whether the Settings UI
shows the option. If FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL doesn't end up
set correctly, the picker shows FHD/HD but selecting them has no
effect - the display stays at native QHD.

This merged patch sets all three flags (FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION,
FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY, FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL) in a
single hunk against the pristine file, plus the VRR resolution-policy
follow-on hunk, so there is no ordering hazard.
---
 smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
index 3619eba0..a1b2c3d4 100644
--- a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
+++ b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
@@ -2835,11 +2835,11 @@
     :goto_e
     sput-boolean v2, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_TSP_DEADZONE_LARGE_FLIP_COVER:Z
 
-    sput-boolean v5, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION:Z
+    sput-boolean v4, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION:Z
 
-    sput-boolean v5, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY:Z
+    sput-boolean v4, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY:Z
 
-    sput-boolean v5, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL:Z
+    sput-boolean v4, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL:Z
 
     const-string v2, "2"
 
@@ -2915,9 +2915,9 @@
 
     sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_VRR_REFRESH_RATE_MODE:Z
 
-    sput-boolean v5, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_VRR_RESOLUTION_POLICY:Z
+    sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_VRR_RESOLUTION_POLICY:Z
 
-    sput-boolean v5, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_VRR_RESOLUTION_POLICY_FOR_SHELL_TRANSITION:Z
+    sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_VRR_RESOLUTION_POLICY_FOR_SHELL_TRANSITION:Z
 
     sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_VRR_FIXED_REFRESH_RATE_PACKAGE:Z
 
